{"summary": "Fixed the API sidebar not rendering on any /api/** page. Root cause: the locale-split refactor injected the per-route API sidebar into page frontmatter (`pageData.frontmatter.sidebar`), but VitePress's default theme only treats `frontmatter.sidebar` as a boolean show/hide flag — actual sidebar content comes exclusively from `themeConfig.sidebar`, resolved per-route via VitePress's `getSidebar()`. Since the locale's `themeConfig.sidebar` only had a guide-prefix key, every API route resolved to an empty sidebar.

Fix in docs/.vitepress/config.ts: merged the already-partitioned `apiSidebarRoutesByLocale[localeKey]` routes into each locale's `themeConfig.sidebar` (VitePress's native multi-path sidebar mechanism) instead of frontmatter, and removed the dead `apiSidebarFor`/`pagePath` helpers and the frontmatter-injection code in `transformPageData`.

Verified via the running dev server that `/api/`, `/api/css/`, and `/guide/getting-started` all render sidebars correctly. Existing api-sidebar tests still pass (7/7)."}
